<title>JAPAN: Japan buys 120,000 tonnes wheat, 80,000 t barley.</title>
<headline>Japan buys 120,000 tonnes wheat, 80,000 t barley.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Japanese Food Agency said on Thursday it had bought 60,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat, 40,000 tonnes of Canadian wheat, 20,000 tonnes of Australian wheat and 80,000 tonnes of Australian barley at its weekly tender, all for November shipment.</p>
<p>The tender results details are as follows, in tonnes.</p>
<p>    Country    Quantity</p>
<p>    U.S.	 60,000	   Western white	    20,000</p>
<p>					Dark northern spring   11,000</p>
<p>					Hard red winter</p>
<p>					 (Ordinary)		 9,000</p>
<p>					 (13 percent protein)  20,000</p>
<p>    Canada     40,000	   1 Canadian western red spring</p>
<p>								     26,000</p>
<p>					Durum			14,000</p>
<p>    Australia  20,000	   Standard white	   20,000</p>
<p>BARLEY</p>
<p>    Country    Quantity</p>
<p>    Australia  80,000	   Feed			 60,000</p>
<p>					Food			 20,000</p>
</text>
